{# LATEST INCIDENTS, ACROSS EVERY AREA — this module's cell on `/`.

   Design: org.widgets.js, the `incidents` cell of the org-overview surface.

   THE CONTRACT, AND NOTHING ELSE. Rendered with `with_context: false` and
   handed ONE map, so everything it reads is under `by.incidents` — the same
   shape this module's partials already read on the area overview.

   ONE READING BEHIND THE TAB AND THE TABLE. The two counts in the tab and the
   rows under them come off the same set, measured once: a card saying seven
   open over rows drawn from a set of eight is the failure that shape exists
   to prevent.

   BOUNDED. Five rows however long the backlog is — the tab says how many
   there are and the door leads to all of them. A dashboard card's height is
   never a function of its data.

   NO WIDGET INDEX. The design prints `IN·G2` in the tab; that is the
   workspace's referencing system and not product. What a reader needs — whose
   figure this is — is the contributor tag.

   → Uhifadhi\Incident\Overview\IncidentOrgWidgets #}
{% set o = by.incidents.org %}
<div class="c" data-w="incidents">
    <span class="tab">Latest incidents<span class="src">&middot; {{ o.cardSubline }}</span></span>
    {% if o.doorUrl %}<a class="more" href="{{ o.doorUrl }}">{{ o.doorLabel }} &rarr;</a>{% endif %}
    <span class="ao-by incidents"><i></i>incidents</span>

    {% if o.latest is empty %}
        <div class="use">{{ o.hasRegister
            ? 'Nothing is open anywhere. Every incident this organization has filed has been seen through.'
            : 'Nothing has been filed anywhere yet. The first incident an area records appears here.' }}</div>
    {% else %}
        <table class="tbl">
            <tr>
                <th>incident</th>
                <th>area</th>
                <th>kind</th>
                <th>filed</th>
                <th>state</th>
            </tr>
            {% for incident in o.latest %}
                <tr>
                    <td><b>{{ incident.reference }}</b></td>
                    <td>{{ incident.area.name }}</td>
                    <td>{{ incident.subcategory.label }}</td>
                    {# The instant carries its own machine value, so the frame
                       prints it in the reader's timezone rather than the
                       server's. #}
                    <td><time datetime="{{ incident.reportedAt|date('c') }}"
                              data-localtime-format="daytime">{{ incident.reportedAt|date('j M H:i') }}</time></td>
                    {# THE RULED CHIP STATES, and no fourth tone of this
                       module's own: past the term it was filed under, inside
                       it but close, or comfortably inside. The term is the
                       sub-category's — one global SLA would be a lie about
                       every category at once. #}
                    <td><span class="chip {{ o.termChip(incident) }}">{{ o.termWords(incident) }}</span></td>
                </tr>
            {% endfor %}
        </table>
    {% endif %}
</div>
